CAT = "llqpConduct"; SEG = "CND"
Q = [
('Under the CCIR/CISRO Fair Treatment of Customers guidance, advice must be based on:',
 "The client's needs and situation", ["The agent's highest commission", "The insurer's sales targets", 'The cheapest product available to them'],
 "Fair treatment puts the customer's interests first: recommendations must fit the needs identified, with clear disclosure."),
('Before recommending a product, an agent must first:',
 'Do a needs analysis', ['Quote the premium', 'Complete the application', 'Collect the first premium'],
 'Knowing the client (finances, goals, family, risk tolerance) comes before any recommendation, and the analysis is documented.'),
("A client is told her old policy \"has no value left\", which is untrue, so that she will switch to a new insurer. The agent is guilty of:",
 'Twisting', ['Rebating', 'Churning', 'Tied selling'],
 'Twisting is inducing a replacement through misrepresentation or an incomplete comparison. It is prohibited in every province.'),
("An agent repeatedly replaces a client's policies mainly to earn new first-year commissions. This is:",
 'Churning', ['Twisting', 'Rebating', 'Rescinding'],
 "Churning is excessive replacement for the agent's gain; the client pays new charges and may lose benefits."),
("An agent promises to pay a client's first three monthly premiums out of his own pocket if she signs today. This inducement is:",
 'Rebating', ['Churning', 'Twisting', 'Defamation'],
 'Rebating is giving a client a benefit not stated in the policy to induce the sale. It is prohibited or restricted in most provinces; rules vary in Quebec and elsewhere.'),
('When an agent recommends replacing an existing life policy, the agent must:',
 'Give a written comparison', ['Cancel the old policy first', "Get the old insurer's approval", 'Avoid mentioning the old policy'],
 'Replacement rules require a disclosure that compares the old and new policies (premiums, surrender charges, new contestable period) so the client decides with full information. Forms vary in Quebec.'),
('A key risk to point out when a client replaces an older policy is that:',
 'A new contestable period starts', ['The old cash value doubles', 'Premiums usually fall to zero', 'The old insurer must pay the client a fee'],
 "A new policy restarts the two-year contestable and suicide periods, and may cost more at the client's higher age."),
("An agent earns a higher commission on one insurer's product than another. Under the guidance, the agent should:",
 'Disclose the conflict to the client', ['Never mention commissions at all', 'Refuse to sell either of the products', 'Let the client guess at it'],
 "Conflicts of interest, including compensation that could influence advice, must be disclosed and managed so they do not override the client's interests."),
("A client asks an agent to backdate an application to get a lower age rate without the insurer's knowledge. The agent should:",
 'Refuse, as it misrepresents', ['Agree if the client pays more', 'Agree for a short backdate', 'Ask a colleague to sign it'],
 'Falsifying an application is misrepresentation and can void coverage and cost the agent the licence. Legitimate backdating is done only by the insurer within its own rules.'),
('Requiring a client to buy life insurance as a condition of getting another product is:',
 'Coercive tied selling', ['A normal package discount', 'A conversion privilege', 'A suitability review'],
 'Tied selling forces a purchase as a condition of another service and is prohibited. Offering a voluntary bundle discount is different.'),
('An elderly client seems confused and is pushed by a relative to cash in her policies. The agent should:',
 'Check her understanding directly', ['Process the request at once', 'Deal only with the relative', 'Cancel her policies to protect her'],
 'With a possibly vulnerable client, the agent takes extra care: speaks with the client directly, checks capacity and understanding, and documents the conversation.'),
('Why should an agent keep detailed notes of every client meeting?',
 'To show what was advised and why', ['To raise the commission', 'Because clients must sign each note', 'To avoid filing applications'],
 'Records of needs, options discussed and reasons for the advice protect both the client and the agent if a complaint or claim arises.'),
('An agent receives a premium cheque from a client. The agent should generally:',
 'Forward it to the insurer promptly', ['Deposit it in a personal account', 'Hold it until the policy is issued', 'Cash it and pay later'],
 'Client money belongs to the client or insurer; mixing it with personal funds (commingling) is prohibited. Trust account rules vary by province.'),
('Which statement to a client about a seg fund breaches market conduct rules?',
 'You cannot lose money in this fund', ['Fees are shown in the Fund Facts', 'The guarantee covers 75% at maturity', 'Values can go down as well as up'],
 'Only the guaranteed portion is protected, at maturity or death; saying there is no risk is a misrepresentation.'),
('A client discloses a past cancer treatment and asks the agent to leave it off the application. The agent should:',
 'Explain it must be disclosed', ['Leave it off as asked', 'Record it in pencil only', 'Tell the client to call the insurer later'],
 'Non-disclosure of a material fact can void the policy within two years and lets a fraud void it at any time. The agent must record the truth.'),
("An agent shares a client's medical details with a friend at a party. This breaches the duty of:",
 'Confidentiality', ['Disclosure', 'Competence', 'Loyalty to the insurer'],
 'Agents must keep client information private and use it only for the purpose it was collected for.'),
("An agent advertises as a 'retirement specialist' but has no training in retirement planning. This is:",
 'Misleading advertising', ['Allowed if the client agrees', 'A normal marketing title', 'Required by most regulators'],
 'Agents must not hold out qualifications or titles they do not have; misleading titles breach conduct rules.'),
('An agent learns that a recommendation she made last year was based on wrong information from the client. Her best step is to:',
 'Review the plan with the client', ['Ignore it since the client erred', 'Cancel the policy herself', 'Report the client to FINTRAC'],
 "An agent's duty continues: when facts change or errors surface, the agent should review the advice and suggest changes where needed."),
('A new client wants coverage far beyond any need the agent can identify and pays with funds from an unknown third party. The agent should:',
 'Ask questions and consider a report', ['Accept the money without asking', 'Return the money silently', 'Double the amount of coverage offered'],
 'Unexplained third-party funds and over-insurance are warning signs. The agent asks about the source, documents it, and reports to FINTRAC if there are grounds to suspect laundering.'),
('When an agent places business with several insurers, the agent should tell the client:',
 'Which insurers the agent represents', ["Only the agent's sales targets", 'Nothing about the insurers used', "The agent's home address and family"],
 'Disclosure of the insurers represented and the nature of the relationship helps the client judge independence. Disclosure forms vary by province.'),
('Why should an agent explain policy exclusions to a client at delivery?',
 'So the client knows the limits', ['Because exclusions void the policy', 'To lower the premium owing', 'Because the regulator signs the policy'],
 'Delivering the policy is the time to review its terms, riders, exclusions and the rescission right, and to answer questions.'),
('A client may usually cancel a newly delivered individual life policy and get a full refund within:',
 '10 days of receiving it', ['2 business days of buying it', '30 days of the medical', '1 year of the issue date'],
 'Individual life policies carry a 10-day free look after delivery for a full premium refund. The two-business-day right applies to seg fund contracts.'),
("An agent wants to email a client's file to an insurer. Under privacy principles, the agent should:",
 'Share only what is needed, securely', ['Copy every client in the email', 'Post it to a shared drive openly', "Delete the client's signed consent form"],
 'Agents limit disclosure to what is needed for the stated purpose and protect information with safeguards suited to its sensitivity.'),
("An agent's incentive is a trip for selling a set amount of one product. Under the Incentive Management Guidance, insurers and agents must:",
 'Manage them so clients are not harmed', ['Hide the incentives from clients', 'Ban every kind of commission', 'Pay the incentive over to the client'],
 'Incentive arrangements must be designed and supervised so they do not lead to unsuitable sales; conflicts are disclosed.'),
]
